<title>GREECE: MYTILINEOS GOES EX-BONUS JANUARY 31.</title>
<headline>MYTILINEOS GOES EX-BONUS JANUARY 31.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece's metals trading company Mytilineos said its bonus shares will be available to shareholders beginning on January 31.</p>
<p>The bonus shares, the outcome of a par value adjustment down to 100 from 250 drachmas will be available in depository receipt form.</p>
<p>Coupon number 2 will entitle shareholders to three new bonus shares for every two outstanding. Thus a shareholder of a 10- share lot will get 15 new shares.</p>
<p>The new shares will also start trading on January 31, the ex-bonus date, and they will be entitled to the fiscal 1996 dividend.</p>
<p>--George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
